"text": " Brazil only needed a draw to win the World Cup at home. July 16th, 1950, the Maracana in Rio. Around 200,000 people by most accounts. There was no final that year, just a group of four. Brazil had beaten Sweden 7-1 and Spain 6-1. Some newspapers were already calling them champions Just after half-time, Friaca scored. 1-0 Brazil. Then Juan Chiafino equalised for Uruguay. One all, still enough for Brazil. With 11 minutes left, Alcides Guilherme ran down the right and shot low inside the near post. 2-1 Uruguay. The whole stadium went silent. Uruguay were world champions. Brazil's goalkeeper, Moashir Barbosa, was blamed for the rest of his life. Biggest shock in World Cup history? Tell me in the comments.",
